    "faq": {
      "kicker": "Patients say",
      "h2": "Two notes left at the desk.",
      "p": "\"I had put off a root canal for two years out of fear. It took two visits and I felt nothing. I wish I had come sooner.\"",
      "span": "· Golpark",
      "p2": "\"My son's braces came off last month. The price we were told on day one is the price we paid. Not one rupee more.\"",
      "span2": "· Ballygunge",
      "kicker2": "Common questions",
      "h22": "Things people ask before they come.",
      "faq": {
        "items": [
          {
            "summary": "Do I need an appointment?",
            "a": "It is better to book, because each dentist has one chair. Send a WhatsApp message or call. If you walk in, you may wait 20 to 40 minutes."
          },
          {
            "summary": "Does a root canal hurt?",
            "a": "The tooth is numbed before anything is done. You feel pressure and vibration, not pain. Mild soreness for a day or two after is normal and a paracetamol is usually enough."
          },
          {
            "summary": "I have diabetes or high blood pressure. Can I get an extraction?",
            "a": "Yes, in most cases. Bring your latest sugar or pressure reading and the list of medicines. If you take a blood thinner we will talk to your physician first."
          },
          {
            "summary": "Is scaling bad for teeth?",
            "a": "No. Scaling removes tartar from the surface; it does not thin the enamel. Teeth can feel sensitive for a few days afterwards because the gums settle back."
          },
          {
            "summary": "How do you sterilise instruments?",
            "a": "Every instrument set is washed, sealed in a pouch and run through the autoclave at 134 degrees. Pouches are opened in front of you. Needles, gloves and suction tips are single use."
          },
          {
            "summary": "Do you take health insurance?",
            "a": "We give a printed bill and treatment summary that most insurers accept for reimbursement. We do not do cashless."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
